
./compile.sh

./install.sh

--

You need to open up the rexec service for this alpha release. On RedHat
you do this by setting the disable parameter to no in the /etc/xinetd.d/rexeci
file and rebooting.

There is a little rexec test program that you can use to make sure that this
is working.

Note: this is a big security hole. So close it back up when done testing.

--

Note: On Solaris in /usr/dt/config/Xservers I had to disable dual head and
 enable 24 bit framebuffer like this:

:0 Local local_uid@console root /usr/openwin/bin/Xsun :0 -nobanner -dev
 /dev/fb0 defdepth 24

I believe this is an SDL issue and not an issue specifically with my code.

